WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.130 --> 00:00:01.210
- This is my first question,

00:00:01.210 --> 00:00:03.520
'cause I know that you
were raised by single mom

00:00:03.520 --> 00:00:04.353
that was a teacher as well.

00:00:04.353 --> 00:00:05.355
- Yes.
- Me as well.

00:00:05.355 --> 00:00:06.380
- My mom taught public
school 5th/6th grade.

00:00:06.380 --> 00:00:07.860
She's retired now
- Yeah.

00:00:07.860 --> 00:00:08.693
- The last couple of years,

00:00:08.693 --> 00:00:10.510
but she wants to see her grandkids more.

00:00:10.510 --> 00:00:11.750
But yeah,
- Yeah

00:00:11.750 --> 00:00:13.190
- She taught public school.

00:00:13.190 --> 00:00:14.260
- Yeah, mine did too.

00:00:14.260 --> 00:00:15.610
And when you went to public school,

00:00:15.610 --> 00:00:16.850
nobody ever did that for me.

00:00:16.850 --> 00:00:18.350
Like Shannon did, like her teacher.

00:00:18.350 --> 00:00:20.090
Did you ever have anything
like that kind of assignment?

00:00:20.090 --> 00:00:22.580
- No, no, not really. I
mean I knew because that

00:00:22.580 --> 00:00:24.160
was my mother's reason for why I couldn't,

00:00:24.160 --> 00:00:26.907
y'know, "can we get the Star Trek toy?"

00:00:26.907 --> 00:00:27.740
"No, we can't afford it."

00:00:27.740 --> 00:00:28.670
It was always we can't afford it.

00:00:28.670 --> 00:00:30.089
- We were broke too.

00:00:30.089 --> 00:00:31.896
- So I just thought like,
"we must be so poor!"

00:00:31.896 --> 00:00:32.729
Y'know? (laughs)
- Yeah. (laughs)

00:00:32.729 --> 00:00:35.380
Because, y'know, she definitely did um,

00:00:35.380 --> 00:00:36.630
well she did have one lesson

00:00:36.630 --> 00:00:39.838
that she kind of tried to
impart to me, growing up.

00:00:39.838 --> 00:00:42.184
Well I really wanted a
dog, when I was a kid.

00:00:42.184 --> 00:00:43.017
- Oh yeah, every kid.

00:00:43.017 --> 00:00:43.850
- It was a lil' little house in Boston.

00:00:43.850 --> 00:00:45.066
Y'know, in they lil' block,

00:00:45.066 --> 00:00:46.150
and it was pretty normal,
near a park, whatever.

00:00:46.150 --> 00:00:47.867
And my mom said,

00:00:47.867 --> 00:00:49.580
"You're not responsible
enough to have a dog."

00:00:49.580 --> 00:00:50.413
I was 10, I was like,

00:00:50.413 --> 00:00:51.850
"I am responsible enough!"

00:00:51.850 --> 00:00:53.120
She said, "You're right.

00:00:53.120 --> 00:00:55.599
Why don't you show me
that you can do this?

00:00:55.599 --> 00:00:58.700
You have to walk the dog
everyday, twice a day."

00:00:58.700 --> 00:00:59.890
I said, "Well okay, let's get the dog!"

00:00:59.890 --> 00:01:00.723
And she goes,

00:01:00.723 --> 00:01:03.379
"No. First, you have to
walk an imaginary dog."

00:01:03.379 --> 00:01:04.380
(crowd laughs)

00:01:04.380 --> 00:01:05.867
- I was like, "Twice? What did you say?"

00:01:05.867 --> 00:01:08.660
"Twice a day, around the
block, as if you had the dog.

00:01:08.660 --> 00:01:10.070
So that I know that you will do it,

00:01:10.070 --> 00:01:11.470
and you're responsible enough to do it."

00:01:11.470 --> 00:01:14.815
So this woman, who I hope is watching,

00:01:14.815 --> 00:01:15.648
- I hope so too!

00:01:15.648 --> 00:01:17.090
- Gave me a leash!

00:01:17.090 --> 00:01:21.190
And I had to walk around the
block with an empty leash.

00:01:21.190 --> 00:01:22.740
- [Kelly] You look nuts!

00:01:22.740 --> 00:01:23.900
- And worse!

00:01:23.900 --> 00:01:26.462
We get to three weeks in, and she's like,

00:01:26.462 --> 00:01:27.295
- [Kelly] (gasps) No!

00:01:27.295 --> 00:01:28.964
"All right, forget it,
I'm not giving you a dog."

00:01:28.964 --> 00:01:30.107
(crowd gasps)

00:01:30.107 --> 00:01:31.378
- No!

00:01:31.378 --> 00:01:32.910
- Yeah, so she taught me the
lesson of disappointment.

00:01:32.910 --> 00:01:34.797
- [Kelly] Ah, yeah. I was like, what?!

00:01:34.797 --> 00:01:36.737
That's like all your
hard work for nothing.

00:01:36.737 --> 00:01:37.570
That is not a good lesson.
- I know.

00:01:37.570 --> 00:01:38.617
- Once she realized, she was like,

00:01:38.617 --> 00:01:40.837
"I didn't think you were
gunna fall through."

00:01:42.105 --> 00:01:43.930
- Oh my God, so you never got the dog.

00:01:43.930 --> 00:01:45.010
- Well I, yeah I didn't get a dog.

00:01:45.010 --> 00:01:47.240
And then I thought I was so deprived,

00:01:47.240 --> 00:01:49.180
I did like the dumbest thing you can do.

00:01:49.180 --> 00:01:50.740
Which you can, that's the kind of thing

00:01:50.740 --> 00:01:52.990
you tend to do when you're
18, which is how old I was.

00:01:52.990 --> 00:01:53.823
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:01:53.823 --> 00:01:56.900
- And I, soon as I moved to
LA and decided to be an actor,

00:01:56.900 --> 00:01:58.820
and had no money and no job.

00:01:58.820 --> 00:02:01.870
I lived in a tiny apartment like on, um,

00:02:01.870 --> 00:02:04.050
Cherokee and Yucca,
over there in Hollywood.

00:02:04.050 --> 00:02:06.685
Like, I was like, "I'm
getting a dog." (laughs)

00:02:06.685 --> 00:02:07.618
(crowd laughs)

00:02:07.618 --> 00:02:08.451
- [Kelly] Dammit

00:02:08.451 --> 00:02:09.530
- So, I went out and got a dog.

00:02:09.530 --> 00:02:11.747
Not only get a dog, but I got a husky.

00:02:11.747 --> 00:02:13.254
(crowd wow's)

00:02:13.254 --> 00:02:14.158
- Which is like, the most,
y'know have anyone had one?

00:02:14.158 --> 00:02:14.991
- That's a hyper dog.

00:02:14.991 --> 00:02:15.824
- They only roam.

00:02:15.824 --> 00:02:16.990
They only want to escape.

00:02:16.990 --> 00:02:18.044
Y'know what I mean?

00:02:18.044 --> 00:02:19.085
That's there, like, mission in life.

00:02:19.085 --> 00:02:19.918
- Yeah.

00:02:19.918 --> 00:02:20.751
- But then I quickly realized like,

00:02:20.751 --> 00:02:22.604
"Oh, you have to get the dog food."

00:02:22.604 --> 00:02:23.437
(laughter)

00:02:23.437 --> 00:02:24.590
- And then like,

00:02:24.590 --> 00:02:25.687
the vet costs money.
- [Kelly] I have to feed it.

00:02:25.687 --> 00:02:28.920
- All of a sudden, I'm kinda
going broke on this dog.

00:02:28.920 --> 00:02:30.700
Ah, has a sad ending to the story though,

00:02:30.700 --> 00:02:33.280
which was that um, I used to leave the dog

00:02:33.280 --> 00:02:34.768
in a little space, shared space,

00:02:34.768 --> 00:02:36.383
in the apartment when I went out.

00:02:36.383 --> 00:02:38.434
So he'd have some outdoor
time, and dog got stolen.

00:02:38.434 --> 00:02:40.691
- That's wrong!

00:02:40.691 --> 00:02:42.540
- This was before the little,

00:02:42.540 --> 00:02:44.250
the microchips and the
stuff you could put in it.

00:02:44.250 --> 00:02:45.503
Y'know you could track 'em down,

00:02:45.503 --> 00:02:46.467
- [Kelly] Yeah, yeah.

00:02:46.467 --> 00:02:47.300
- and yeah so somebody stole the dog.

00:02:47.300 --> 00:02:49.336
But, it's telling that I didn't rush out

00:02:49.336 --> 00:02:51.070
and get another dog.

00:02:51.070 --> 00:02:51.903
- Yeah, right.

00:02:51.903 --> 00:02:53.460
You were like, "You know
what, the universe knew."

00:02:53.460 --> 00:02:54.340
- Whoa, yeah.

00:02:54.340 --> 00:02:55.784
Somebody has spoken and this is probably,

00:02:55.784 --> 00:02:56.820
he probably was not living
his best life with me.

00:02:56.820 --> 00:02:58.143
- [Kelly] I did the same thing.

00:02:58.143 --> 00:03:00.939
- I'm sure he has a very
happy life, on a farm,

00:03:00.939 --> 00:03:02.721
in Montana somewhere.

00:03:02.721 --> 00:03:04.430
- I did the same thing though.

00:03:04.430 --> 00:03:05.390
When I was young, I was like;

00:03:05.390 --> 00:03:07.040
I think you, when you're out here,

00:03:07.040 --> 00:03:08.050
'cause I moved out here too

00:03:08.050 --> 00:03:10.080
and you want companionship
or some kind of,

00:03:10.080 --> 00:03:11.240
you can't be lonely.

00:03:11.240 --> 00:03:12.210
So I did that too.

00:03:12.210 --> 00:03:13.333
It was a dumb move.

00:03:13.333 --> 00:03:14.166
- Yeah, and it's like,

00:03:14.166 --> 00:03:15.413
- [Kelly] I ended up having a
friend take care of the dog.

00:03:15.413 --> 00:03:16.560
- When you have the least
money, the smallest place.

00:03:16.560 --> 00:03:18.050
- [Kelly] You make the poorest decisions.

00:03:18.050 --> 00:03:19.160
- And you're the dumbest!

00:03:19.160 --> 00:03:22.160
Well like, let me find another
life that could depend on me.

00:03:23.140 --> 00:03:25.172
- 'Cause I'm holding it
down solidly like myself.

00:03:25.172 --> 00:03:26.669
- [Ben Affleck] (laughing)
Because I have it taken care of.

